    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining our offensive attack, both surging past the 73.0 efficiency mark. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 14% dynamic platoon advantage against Yesavage, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is positioned to exploit a favorable matchup against Merrill Kelly, whose 4.74 xERA remains a prime target for our middle infielders. Despite the scarcity of stolen bases league-wide, **Nasim Nunez** maintains a strong 60.8 score today; while hitting in the 9-hole suppresses his ceiling, the combination of Kelly\u2019s glacial delivery\u2014allowing for high-percentage swipes\u2014and the overall team matchup keeps him firmly in the UTIL slot to secure those critical category points. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** rounds out our elite tier, carrying a 72.3 score into his matchup against Young, buoyed by a robust .371 xwOBA that signals he is due for significant production.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Josh Jung**, who ultimately sat at a 44.49 efficiency score. While **Josh Jung** projects well enough for a standard start, he was edged out by the superior platoon leverage offered by the starters facing weaker pitching. Our strategy today intentionally de-prioritizes bats like **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci** against Luzardo, whose 3.22 xERA presents a significant hurdle that drags their efficiency scores into the marginal range. We are also monitoring the risk surrounding **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**; both face Detmers, whose 3.21 xERA makes him the toughest arm we\u2019ll see today. While **Andy Pages** receives a minor boost for his speed potential on the basepaths, the overall SP skill factor caps the expectations for both outfielders. We remain vigilant on **Jordan Westburg**\u2019s status as he continues his recovery, but for tonight, the lineup is optimized to maximize run-scoring potential while maintaining our competitive edge in the scarcity-driven SB category.",
